00:17:10.069 --> 00:17:11.440
Say I'm a developer.

00:17:11.440 --> 00:17:14.119
I'm working on Google
Cloud Platform.

00:17:14.119 --> 00:17:21.030
Is there anything that I can do
to put in place these practices

00:17:21.030 --> 00:17:22.359
as I'm building my application?

00:17:22.359 --> 00:17:24.920
Are there tools or
agents or anything

00:17:24.920 --> 00:17:26.890
that I should be
doing from the outset?

00:17:26.890 --> 00:17:29.860
Maybe for some of those things,
more like GCE or other stuff.

00:17:29.860 --> 00:17:31.860
MORGAN MCLEAN: Yeah,
so I know this touches

00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:32.693
on a previous point.

00:17:32.693 --> 00:17:34.349
If you're using App
Engine, of course,

00:17:34.349 --> 00:17:35.890
you're getting all
this functionality

00:17:35.890 --> 00:17:37.449
for free, basically, right?

00:17:37.449 --> 00:17:39.740
The beauty of it is that you
don't have to think ahead.

00:17:39.740 --> 00:17:41.490
You don't have to start
linking libraries,

00:17:41.490 --> 00:17:44.880
or go to a third party
solution or anything like that.

00:17:44.880 --> 00:17:47.980
If you're a developer,
