00:17:58.720 --> 00:18:01.470
and you'll go to the Trace
panel on Cloud Console

00:18:01.470 --> 00:18:05.140
and you won't see any traces
because we didn't capture any.

00:18:05.140 --> 00:18:08.110
But if you look at the
Trace documentation

00:18:08.110 --> 00:18:10.880
on the Google Cloud
Platform website,

00:18:10.880 --> 00:18:12.920
we have links there
to our Java library,

00:18:12.920 --> 00:18:15.840
and an OJS library for Trace,
and links for Python and Go

00:18:15.840 --> 00:18:17.350
should be arriving shortly.

00:18:17.350 --> 00:18:20.430
And those are libraries that you
can integrate with your code.

00:18:20.430 --> 00:18:22.980
And depending on the
library and depending

00:18:22.980 --> 00:18:25.390
on when you're
listening to this,

00:18:25.390 --> 00:18:27.380
we'll have different
levels of support.

00:18:27.380 --> 00:18:30.254
But already today, if
you're using an OJS library,

00:18:30.254 --> 00:18:31.670
for example, you
link the library.

00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:34.060
You get it through NPM
in your application,

00:18:34.060 --> 00:18:36.250
and suddenly, you're
collecting traces.

00:18:36.250 --> 00:18:39.430
Some of the other ones like
Java, the initial release,

00:18:39.430 --> 00:18:42.010
you'll have to sprinkle
it throughout your code.

00:18:42.010 --> 00:18:43.359
And so it's not just linking it.

00:18:43.359 --> 00:18:44.900
There's a little
more work than that.

00:18:44.900 --> 00:18:46.858
And so that is something
you should think about

00:18:46.858 --> 00:18:47.910
while you're developing.

00:18:47.910 --> 00:18:49.660
We hope to move beyond
that in the future,

00:18:49.660 --> 00:18:52.160
but that's where we are today.

00:18:52.160 --> 00:18:54.000
So yeah, if you're on
GCE, GKE, and you're

00:18:54.000 --> 00:18:56.040
using Java or a
language other than Node

00:18:56.040 --> 00:18:57.664
and you want to use
Trace and, I think,

00:18:57.664 --> 00:19:00.290
some of the other features, you
should be thinking about this.

00:19:00.290 --> 00:19:02.790
And you should be thinking about
the telemetry that you want

00:19:02.790 --> 00:19:05.123
to collect, the instrumentation
that you want to send us

00:19:05.123 --> 00:19:07.010
and that we can provide
to you, and focus

00:19:07.010 --> 00:19:08.654
on what's the most useful.

00:19:08.654 --> 00:19:10.320
If Trace is very
useful to you, then you

00:19:10.320 --> 00:19:12.900
should go use one of those
libraries and sprinkle it in.

00:19:12.900 --> 00:19:15.630
SHARAT SHROFF: Yeah, I think
much of what Morgan said

00:19:15.630 --> 00:19:18.910
